    {
      "crop_slug": "shallot",
      "field_path": "start_method.notes_beginner",
      "our_prose": "The easy way to grow shallots is from sets, which are small bulbs you buy and plant. Each set splits into a clump of several bulbs. Push each set in pointy-end up so the tip just shows at the soil surface, and space them at their final distance because shallots are not thinned. Pick firm sets and avoid big or already-sprouting ones, which tend to flower instead of dividing. You can also grow shallots from seed, started indoors about 8 to 10 weeks early, which gives single bulbs rather than clumps.",
      "run_normalized": "from sets which are small bulbs",
      "run_in_our_prose": "from sets, which are small bulbs",
